{number: 36}
{title: He Lives}
{key: Bb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Bb] I serve a risen Savior, He's in the world today;
I know that He is living, whatever [F7] men may say;
I [Bb] see His hand of mercy, I hear His voice of cheer,
And [C7] just the time I need Him He's [F7] always near.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
He [Bb] lives, He lives, Christ Jesus lives today!
He [F7] walks with me and [Bb] talks with me a-[C7] long life's narrow [F7] way.
He [Bb] lives, He [Bb7] lives, sal-[Eb] vation to im-[G7] part!
You [C7] ask me how I know He lives?
He [Bb] lives with-[F7] in my [Bb] heart.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
In [Bb] all the world around me I see His loving care,
And though my heart grows weary I never [F7] will despair;
I [Bb] know that He is leading thro' all the stormy blast,
The [C7] day of His appearing will [F7] come at last.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Re-[Bb] joice, rejoice, O Christian, lift up your voice and sing
Eternal hallelujahs to Jesus [F7] Christ the King!
The [Bb] Hope of all who seek Him, the Help of all who find,
None [C7] other is so loving, so [F7] good and kind.
{end_of_verse}
